        "original_id": "84240949-f5db-51fe-a4f2-d1674f99bce8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Tarrero-Serrano, Carlos Prio, Fulgencio Batista, Osvaldo Farrés\n- Roles: Cuban President, Cuban First Lady\n- Places: Cuba\n- Events: military coup, Cuban Revolution\n- Works: “Quizás, Quizás, Quizás”\n\nFacts:\n- Fulgencio Batista was born as Rubén Zaldívar on January 16, 1901.\n- Fulgencio Batista was the elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944.\n- Mary Tarrero-Serrano was the second wife of Cuban President Carlos Prio.\n- Carlos Prio was overthrown by Fulgencio Batista in a military coup.\n- Fulgencio Batista was a U.S.-backed dictator of Cuba from 1952 to 1959.\n- Osvaldo Farrés received help and inspiration for the lyrics of “Quizás, Quizás, Quizás” from Cuban First Lady Mary Tarrero-Serrano.\n- Fulgencio Batista was overthrown during the Cuban Revolution.\n- Fulgencio Batista died on August 6, 1973.",
